//! \defgroup core_api Core API
//! \brief Everything you need to control a Robotiq gripper over a real
//! connection.
//!
//! **Start with Gripper — everything else in this group exists to build
//! one, feed it, or read it back.** There is exactly one class to drive;
//! the rest are the data it moves and the pieces it is built from.
//!
//! \code
//!               ConnectionConfig                Serial + Platform + Logger
//!             (SerialConfig + slave addr)      (custom transport, RTOS port,
//!                     |                          or a test double)
//!                     |    construct()                |    construct()
//!                     |    (built-in serial)           |    (bring your own)
//!                     +----------------+----------------+
//!                                      v
//!                             +-----------------+
//!                             |     Gripper     |   <- the class you drive
//!                             +-----------------+
//!                            /         |         \
//!                 setCommand()   getStatus()   connectionState()
//!                       /             |             \
//!                      v              v              v
//!             GripperCommand   GripperStatus   ConnectionState
//!               (you send)     (FaultStatus
//!                                lives inside)
//! \endcode
//!
//! activate() and recoverFromFault() are free functions layered on top of
//! those same accessors — not members — so Gripper itself never blocks;
//! they poll with the waitFor()/waitUntil() helpers from **Utilities**,
//! which your own code can use the same way.
//!
//!   - **Commands & Status** — the typed blocks Gripper exchanges
//!     (GripperCommand out, GripperStatus in) and the fault codes they carry.
//!   - **Connection & Configuration** — how a Gripper is told what to
//!     connect to, and what state that connection is in.
//!   - **Runtime & Extension Points** — the injectable pieces (Serial,
//!     Platform, Logger) Gripper is built on, for custom transports,
//!     RTOS targets, and tests.
//!   - **Utilities** — small, independent helpers used while driving a
//!     Gripper (bit flags, rate limiting, polling).
//!
//! See \ref testing "Testing & CI Utilities" for driving this same API
//! without a physical gripper attached.

//! \defgroup commanding Commands & Status
//! \ingroup core_api
//! \brief The typed command and status blocks a Gripper exchanges with
//! the hardware, and the fault codes carried in the status block.

//! \defgroup connection Connection & Configuration
//! \ingroup core_api
//! \brief How a Gripper is configured, and the state of its connection.

//! \defgroup runtime Runtime & Extension Points
//! \ingroup core_api
//! \brief The injectable transport, platform, and logging interfaces
//! Gripper is built on — implement these to add a custom transport, port
//! to an RTOS, or capture logs in tests.

//! \defgroup utilities Utilities
//! \ingroup core_api
//! \brief Small, independent helpers used while driving a Gripper.

//! \defgroup testing Testing & CI Utilities
//! \brief Tools for exercising the SDK without a physical gripper attached.
//!
//! Not part of the real control path — see \ref core_api "Core API" for that.
